 ## Safety model
 
-The migration installer reads all 8 MiB before writing anything, preserves the
-existing NVS data, and changes only Wi-Fi and `wifi.ota_url`. The v2 layout is
-not OTA-compatible with the legacy v1 layout, so the first migration must use
-USB. Do not run it until the controlled HTTPS OTA relay and release manifest
-have been deployed.
-
-Use a real 8 MiB backup from an original AI04 to validate the NVS patcher
-before first-device use. The included automated tests use synthetic NVS pages
-and cannot substitute for that device-specific check.
-
-## OTA relay
-
-Set the relay's `XIAOZHI_UPSTREAM_URL` to the current official default,
-`https://api.tenclass.net/xiaozhi/ota/`, and set `AI04_MANIFEST_URL` to the
-controlled HTTPS manifest that serves the release `xiaozhi.bin`. The official
-cloud firmware builder cannot compile this reconstructed board until the board
-definition has been merged upstream.
+The migration installer reads all 8 MiB before writing anything and validates
+the exact factory AI04 table: `model` at `0x10000`, `ota_0` at `0x100000`, and
+`ota_1` at `0x480000`. It preserves the bootloader, partition table, model
+data and inactive app slot. It changes only Wi-Fi/`wifi.ota_url` plus the
+currently selected OTA application slot, so the original boot selection remains
+valid. The installer writes the official XiaoZhi activation/configuration URL;
+the compiled AI04 firmware reads its PT-BR update offer only from the controlled
+HTTPS manifest.
+
+Use a real 8 MiB backup from an original AI04 to validate both the NVS patcher
+and stock-layout detector before first-device use. The included automated tests
+use synthetic data and cannot substitute for that device-specific check.
+Never commit or publish that raw backup: its NVS may contain Wi-Fi credentials
+and activation tokens.
+
+## Native OTA channel
+
+For the AI04 only, the native firmware always contacts
+`https://api.tenclass.net/xiaozhi/ota/` for activation, MQTT/WebSocket settings
+and time. It then reads `CONFIG_AI04_OTA_MANIFEST_URL` without transmitting
+device identity. A valid manifest replaces the official firmware offer; a
+missing or invalid manifest removes the firmware offer entirely. That
+fail-closed behavior prevents an English image from being installed.
+
+The official cloud firmware builder cannot compile this reconstructed board
+until the board definition has been merged upstream.
